{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CCD",
    "description": "Space Domain Awareness (SDA) classification exercise. Operator teams fly a shared TWO-spacecraft observation network - one LEO 'Overwatch' node and one GEO node - and must detect, track, image and CLASSIFY a curated field of target spacecraft/objects using photometry (CCD/optical) and radar. Each team flies one LEO node (a wide-field survey 'Overwatch' craft at ~900 km / SMA 7278 km - a higher LEO chosen so ground-station footprints overlap and coverage is near-continuous) and one GEO node. TARGETS ARE MODELLED TWO WAYS: (a) 'neutral' assets (top-level assets.neutral[]) that spawn as real, team-less spacecraft so they can carry a real rendered visualization.reflectivity and a real physics.attitude_rate (tumble); and (b) passive objects.space[] for targets that only need position (radar-only, eclipse, size-mismatch, dead sats). GROUPS: (G1) a 6-satellite LEO constellation placed CO-ORBITAL and leading the LEO Overwatch node (same plane/period, ~12 deg ahead) so all six sit in the velocity/ram field of view continuously - operators just hold velocity pointing - with (G2) two disguised members carrying an anomalous reflectivity so participants can pick them out; (G3) three SLOWLY-tumbling rocket bodies in the GEO belt, each given a real physics.attitude_rate so their brightness varies periodically over ~80-180 s, with enlarged scale; plus two GEO-neighbourhood objects for the GEO node - (G4) a co-orbital companion on a near-identical relative orbit to the GEO spacecraft, and (G5) a retrograde 'interloper' on an opposite-direction orbit that makes its closest approach to the GEO spacecraft ~45 minutes into the run. NOTE: visualization.reflectivity and physics.attitude_rate are REAL engine fields (assets only). The per-object 'diameter'/'albedo'/'spectral_albedo'/'specularity'/'luminosity'/'catalog_class' and the observer 'Radar' component remain forward-looking descriptors. 'truth' blocks are instructor ground-truth only. Verify view windows, eclipse timing and continuous ground coverage with a dry run and tune the station set / min_elevation accordingly."
  },
